<title>GERMANY: Continental higher after strong H1 results.</title>
<headline>Continental higher after strong H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German tyre-maker Continental were boosted on Tuesday when the company said its 1996 first half pre-tax profits more than doubled to 120 million marks, in line with analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>Shares in the world's fourth-largest tyre maker were up 28 pfennigs at 25.20 marks, over one percent, in mid-session bourse trade, while the overall market was up 2.68 points, or 0.10 percent, at 2,555.04 points.</p>
<p>News that Continental expected higher full-year profitability also helped lift the share.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
